              "alt": {
                "segmentId": "m00285:alt:OChem_23_10_004e_jpg-alt",
                "text": "The structure of propenenitrile (acrylonitrile) shows a three-carbon chain where the first carbon is triple-bonded to nitrogen. A double bond is shared between the second and third carbon atoms.",
                "mediaId": null,
                "src": "../../media/OChem_23_10_004e.jpg"
              }
            },
            {
